      "composition": "single-ornament",
      "description": "A wide gray acanthus ornament from the lower margin of the calendar frame. Three large curling stems, a spiral at the left, a tall S-bend in the middle and a spiral at the right, grow from a common root at the bottom centre and throw off smaller folded and hooked leaves with pale knobs; the leaves are blue-gray with white highlights and darker gray shadows. Transparent background, the stems ending where they met the frame's flowers.",
